<text>
    <body>
        <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_11">Paris</name> <dateline>
                                    <date when="1923-02-16">16.2.23</date>
                                </dateline> </addrLine>
<addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_11">26 avenue Charles Floquet</name> </addrLine>
<addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_11">VII<hi rend="superscript">ème</hi>
                                </name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab> </div>

<div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear<name type="person" key="weav76"> Miss Weaver</name>, </p>
<p>
                        <rs type="person" key="joyc82">My father</rs> asks me to tell you that the <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">dionine-treatment</seg> was begun on <choice>
                            <sic>thursday</sic>
                            <corr>Thursday</corr>
                        </choice> and continued yesterday. He is to go again to-day but it will not be possible to know if it had a good effect for some days. Unfortunately there seems to be since yesterday some trouble in the other eye but <rs type="person" key="bors73">the doctor</rs> thinks it will not develop. </p>
<p>
                        <rs type="person" key="joyc82">My father</rs> was not able to continue the corrections as you wish because the <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">copy</seg> from <name type="person" key="rodk94">Mr. Rodker</name> arrived only to-day but as soon as this experiment is over he will continue them here and in the hospital. </p>
<closer>
                        <salute>With best greetings, </salute>
<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>

</div>
</div>

<div type="notes">
<note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ began dionine treatment with <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Dr Louis Colin</name> in <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_NICE">Nice</name> in the autumn of 1922 and continued it with Dr Borsch. Rather than heeding Colin’s recommendation for a “strong solution”, Borsch “prefers to continue the treatment gradually and to wait and see if the film will thin more” according to a <rs type="letter" key="L_68967">letter from JJ to Weaver on <date when="1923-02-26">26 February 1923</date>
                    </rs> (<name type="work">LIII</name> 72). See <rs type="letter" key="L_68945">letter to Harriet Weaver, 13 November 1922</rs> for JJ’s early mention of dionine treatment in Nice. </note>

<note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">In <date when="1923-01">January 1923</date>, John Rodker printed an additional 500 copies of the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Egoist Press</name> edition of <hi rend="italic">
                        <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>
                    </hi> that had been published in <date when="1922-10">October 1922</date>.</note>

</div>
</body>
